\title{Structured terms inside a tobs() formula}
\description{
Spatial fields, random effects, temporal structure, varying coefficients and
latent factors are written inside the model formula, in the process they
belong to, rather than passed as \code{tobs()} arguments. A term entered in
the state formula acts on occupancy or abundance; the same term written in
\code{detection = ~ ...} acts on detection.
}
\details{
These are formula specials, not exported functions: they are resolved
against an internal registry while the formula is parsed, and calling them
outside a \code{tobs()} formula is an error. This page documents the call
shapes and their arguments.
